※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4591

※ `⎕widen` answers the value itself and not a result, which it may do only
※ because it cannot fail.  A signed type goes into no unsigned one: a negative
※ number is somewhere the unsigned type does not reach, so this is a narrowing
※ and `⎕narrow` is what answers whether it fitted.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let b: i64 = ⁻3i64
    let q: u64 = ⎕widen(b, ⌜u64⌝)
    if q = 0u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
